        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-18T14:43:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At this stage we\u0027re mostly targeting demos/samples to lure people into using SkParticles.  Longer term it would be nice to have a clean solution for something like an image (or shader) uniform.\n\nUnpacking to an atlas sounds like a neat optimization, but some of the assets might be fairly large.  Think generic video, or even something like a camera feed which cannot be pre-rendered.\n\nIt just occurred to be that all image loading is already routed through a ResourceProvider, so I we could move the image setup hack to a custom provider/image asset, and just use the existing SkImageBinding (we just need a way to hijack the SkImage creation).",
      "parentUuid": "531d4dcc_ea751ba4",
